---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Rete neurale: una pagina che si legge dall'alto, un concetto per capitolo. La rete è vera e si allena nel browser (src/lib/rete.ts)
---
<Base title="Neural network · Riccardo Mondi" description="Add neurons one at a time and watch a small neural network learn to draw, in your browser." largo>
  <main class="rn" data-rete>
    <p class="mono via"><a href="/">~</a>/<a href="/learn/">learn</a>/neural-network</p>
    <h1>How does a neural network learn to draw?</h1>
    <p class="testo">This is a real neural network, running in your browser. It is also a simplified one: it reads a position on a grid and answers with one number, a height. Its goal is to raise the shape of a fish out of a flat grid, drawn here in blue.</p>

    <section class="capitolo" data-capitolo="uno" data-invito="">
      <h2 class="mono">1 · One neuron</h2>
      <p class="testo">A neuron multiplies each input by a weight, adds the results, and squashes the sum between 0 and 1. On our grid, that makes one straight step. Move the two squares and try to cover the fish. One step is all that a neuron can make.</p>
      <div class="scena">
        <canvas class="tela-rete" role="img" aria-label="One neuron with two inputs, x and y"></canvas>
        <canvas class="tela-terreno" role="img" aria-label="A wire grid with one straight step, and two squares that move it"></canvas>
      </div>
      <p class="mono comandi"><span class="lettura"></span></p>
      <p class="mono dettaglio"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="capitolo" data-capitolo="neuroni">
      <h2 class="mono">2 · More neurons</h2>
      <p class="testo">Now each neuron makes its own step, and the last neuron adds them up. The sum is no longer straight: it starts to look like a shape. Add neurons one at a time. Each one trains together with the others.</p>
      <div class="scena">
        <canvas class="tela-rete" role="img" aria-label="Network with one layer of neurons"></canvas>
        <canvas class="tela-terreno" role="img" aria-label="A wire grid where the shape rises as you add neurons"></canvas>
      </div>
      <p class="mono comandi">
        <button type="button" class="meno" aria-label="Remove a neuron" disabled>−</button>
        <span class="numero">1</span>
        <button type="button" class="piu primo" aria-label="Add a neuron">+ neuron</button>
        <span class="lettura"></span>
      </p>
      <p class="mono dettaglio"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="capitolo" data-capitolo="strati">
      <h2 class="mono">3 · Layers</h2>
      <p class="testo">Same number of neurons, in a different order. A neuron in a second layer does not read the position: it reads the steps of the first layer, and combines them into corners and plateaus. Add a layer and compare the match. Then hover a neuron in the last layer: it is no longer a straight step.</p>
      <div class="scena">
        <canvas class="tela-rete" role="img" aria-label="Network with sixteen neurons arranged in layers"></canvas>
        <canvas class="tela-terreno" role="img" aria-label="A wire grid with the shape made by the network"></canvas>
      </div>
      <p class="mono comandi">
        <button type="button" class="meno" aria-label="Remove a layer" disabled>−</button>
        <span class="numero">16 neurons in 1 layer</span>
        <button type="button" class="piu primo" aria-label="Add a layer">+ layer</button>
        <span class="lettura"></span>
      </p>
      <p class="mono dettaglio"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="capitolo" data-capitolo="impara">
      <h2 class="mono">4 · How it learns</h2>
      <p class="testo">Nobody sets those weights by hand. The network starts at random and repeats three moves: it tries a point, compares the answer with the right one, and corrects its weights a little. Press step to see one correction, slowly. Press play to see thousands.</p>
      <div class="scena">
        <canvas class="tela-rete" role="img" aria-label="Network with values that travel forward and corrections that travel back"></canvas>
        <canvas class="tela-terreno" role="img" aria-label="A wire grid that goes from random to the shape of the fish"></canvas>
      </div>
      <p class="mono comandi">
        <button type="button" class="gioca primo">play</button>
        <button type="button" class="un-passo">step</button>
        <button type="button" class="azzera">restart</button>
        <span class="fasi" aria-hidden="true"><span>1 try</span><span>2 compare</span><span>3 correct</span></span>
        <span class="lettura"></span>
      </p>
      <p class="mono dettaglio"></p>
      <div class="mono andamento"><span class="errore"></span><canvas class="curva" role="img" aria-label="The error over time"></canvas></div>
      <p class="testo nota-termini">The two names you will hear: sending the error back through the network is <em>backpropagation</em>. Moving each weight in the direction that lowers the error is <em>gradient descent</em>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="capitolo" data-capitolo="libero">
      <h2 class="mono">5 · Your turn</h2>
      <p class="testo">Pick a shape or draw your own, then build the network. Thin shapes and corners need more neurons. Drag the grid to turn it.</p>
      <div class="scena">
        <canvas class="tela-rete" role="img" aria-label="The network you built"></canvas>
        <canvas class="tela-terreno" role="img" aria-label="A wire grid with the shape you chose"></canvas>
      </div>
      <p class="mono comandi">
        <button type="button" data-sagoma="fish">fish</button>
        <button type="button" data-sagoma="fir">fir</button>
        <button type="button" data-sagoma="bird">bird</button>
        <button type="button" class="matita">draw your own</button>
        <button type="button" class="pulisci" hidden>clear</button>
      </p>
      <p class="mono comandi">
        <span class="etichetta-c">layers</span>
        <button type="button" class="strati-meno" aria-label="Remove a layer">−</button><span class="strati-n"></span><button type="button" class="strati-piu" aria-label="Add a layer">+</button>
        <span class="etichetta-c">neurons per layer</span>
        <button type="button" class="neuroni-meno" aria-label="Remove a neuron from each layer">−</button><span class="neuroni-n"></span><button type="button" class="neuroni-piu" aria-label="Add a neuron to each layer">+</button>
        <span class="lettura"></span>
      </p>
      <p class="mono dettaglio"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="capitolo chiusura">
      <h2 class="mono">What is simplified</h2>
      <p class="testo">This network has two inputs and at most a few dozen neurons, and it trains on one shape. A large model reads text or images, has billions of weights, and trains for weeks on huge machines. The moves are the same: weighted sums, steps, layers, an error, and small corrections.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<script>
  import { monta } from '../../scripts/reteVista';
  monta(document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-rete]')!);
</script>

<style>
  .rn { max-width: 1040px; padding-top: var(--s1); }
  .via { margin: 0; }
  .via a { color: inherit; }
  h1 { margin: var(--s1) 0 var(--s2); font-size: 33px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; }
  .testo { max-width: 660px; margin: 0 0 var(--s2); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .testo em { font-style: normal; color: var(--arancio); }
  .capitolo { padding: var(--s4) 0 var(--s2); }
  .capitolo h2 { margin: 0 0 var(--s1); font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .scena { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.7fr); gap: var(--s2); align-items: stretch; }
  .tela-rete, .tela-terreno { display: block; width: 100%; height: 400px; touch-action: pan-y; }
  .tela-terreno { cursor: grab; }
  .tela-terreno:active { cursor: grabbing; }
  button { padding: 1px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg); color: var(--muted); font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
  button:hover:not(:disabled) { color: var(--fg); border-color: var(--muted); }
  button:disabled { opacity: .4; cursor: default; }
  button[hidden] { display: none; }
  button[aria-pressed="true"] { border-color: var(--fg); color: var(--fg); }
  .primo { border-color: var(--fg); color: var(--fg); }
  .primo:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--fg); color: var(--bg); }
  .comandi { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 10px; align-items: center; margin: var(--s1) 0 0; color: var(--fg); }
  .lettura { margin-left: auto; font-size: 15px; color: var(--fg); }
  .etichetta-c { color: var(--muted); }
  .etichetta-c:not(:first-child) { margin-left: var(--s1); }
  .dettaglio { min-height: 34px; margin: var(--s1) 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .fasi { display: inline-flex; gap: 4px; margin-left: var(--s1); }
  .fasi span { padding: 1px 6px; border: 1px solid transparent; color: var(--muted); opacity: .6; }
  .fasi span.accesa { opacity: 1; border-color: var(--fg); color: var(--fg); }
  .andamento { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px var(--s2); align-items: center; margin-bottom: var(--s2); color: var(--muted); }
  .curva { flex: 1 1 200px; min-width: 160px; height: 34px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .nota-termini { color: var(--muted); }
  .chiusura { padding-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    /* Su telefono prima la griglia: è quella che cambia quando tocchi i comandi */
    .scena { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .tela-terreno { order: -1; height: 300px; }
    .tela-rete { height: 230px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    h1 { font-size: 24px; }
    .capitolo { padding-top: var(--s3); }
    button { padding: 6px 12px; }
    .lettura { margin-left: 0; width: 100%; }
    .fasi { width: 100%; margin-left: 0; }
  }
</style>
